    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This podcast hopes to help the general public understand archery as a sport and not just as a media trope. Through both the narrator’s personal experience as a collegiate archer on the Stanford archery team as well as drawing from sources that explain the psychological effects the sport has on athletes, the podcast will provide an in-depth exploration into the world of competitive archery. There will be a brief overview of the sport itself; most of the podcast will be devoted to the unique psychological challenges that archery carries, which sets it apart from other sports. Interview with Stanford Archery's head coach, Francis Parchaso.",
